    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "s = \"aba\"     ->  true    (already a palindrome)\ns = \"abca\"    ->  true    (delete \"b\" or \"c\")\ns = \"abc\"     ->  false   (needs two deletions)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: the first mismatch decides"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Walk two pointers inwards as in Valid Palindrome. While the pairs match, nothing needs deleting. At the **first** mismatch, the deletion must happen right there — every pair outside it already matches and must stay matched. So there are only two choices: delete the **left** character or the **right** one. Check whether either leaves a palindrome between the pointers. No other position ever needs trying."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Brute force: try deleting every character"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If the string is already a palindrome, done. Otherwise build every string with one character removed and test each."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function validPalindrome(s) {\n  const isPal = (t) => t === [...t].reverse().join(\"\");\n  if (isPal(s)) return true;                 // no deletion needed\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n    if (isPal(s.slice(0, i) + s.slice(i + 1))) return true;   // try deleting s[i]\n  }\n  return false;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def valid_palindrome(s):\n    if s == s[::-1]:\n        return True                       # no deletion needed\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        t = s[:i] + s[i + 1:]             # try deleting s[i]\n        if t == t[::-1]:\n            return True\n    return False"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "boolean validPalindrome(String s) {\n    if (isPal(s)) return true;                   // no deletion needed\n    for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\n        if (isPal(s.substring(0, i) + s.substring(i + 1))) return true;   // try deleting s[i]\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n\nboolean isPal(String t) {\n    return new StringBuilder(t).reverse().toString().equals(t);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "bool isPal(const string& t) {\n    return equal(t.begin(), t.end(), t.rbegin());\n}\n\nbool validPalindrome(string s) {\n    if (isPal(s)) return true;                   // no deletion needed\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < s.size(); i++) {\n        if (isPal(s.substr(0, i) + s.substr(i + 1))) return true;   // try deleting s[i]\n    }\n    return false;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n²), space O(n).** n candidate strings, each built and checked in O(n)."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Two pointers, two tries at the first mismatch"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Match pairs from the outside in. At the first mismatch, return whether `s[left+1..right]` **or** `s[left..right-1]` is a palindrome — two quick checks of the part that's left."
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "valid-palindrome-ii",
      "caption": "Pairs match from the outside; at the first mismatch, skip the left character, then if needed the right one."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function validPalindrome(s) {\n  const isPal = (i, j) => {                  // is s[i..j] a palindrome?\n    while (i < j) {\n      if (s[i] !== s[j]) return false;\n      i++;\n      j--;\n    }\n    return true;\n  };\n  let left = 0, right = s.length - 1;\n  while (left < right) {\n    if (s[left] !== s[right]) {\n      // One deletion allowed: drop the left character or the right one, and check the rest.\n      return isPal(left + 1, right) || isPal(left, right - 1);\n    }\n    left++;\n    right--;\n  }\n  return true;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def valid_palindrome(s):\n    def is_pal(i, j):                     # is s[i..j] a palindrome?\n        while i < j:\n            if s[i] != s[j]:\n                return False\n            i += 1\n            j -= 1\n        return True\n\n    left, right = 0, len(s) - 1\n    while left < right:\n        if s[left] != s[right]:\n            # One deletion allowed: drop the left character or the right one, and check the rest.\n            return is_pal(left + 1, right) or is_pal(left, right - 1)\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n    return True"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "boolean validPalindrome(String s) {\n    int left = 0, right = s.length() - 1;\n    while (left < right) {\n        if (s.charAt(left) != s.charAt(right)) {\n            // One deletion allowed: drop the left character or the right one, and check the rest.\n            return isPal(s, left + 1, right) || isPal(s, left, right - 1);\n        }\n        left++;\n        right--;\n    }\n    return true;\n}\n\nboolean isPal(String s, int i, int j) {          // is s[i..j] a palindrome?\n    while (i < j) {\n        if (s.charAt(i) != s.charAt(j)) return false;\n        i++;\n        j--;\n    }\n    return true;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "bool isPal(const string& s, int i, int j) {      // is s[i..j] a palindrome?\n    while (i < j) {\n        if (s[i] != s[j]) return false;\n        i++;\n        j--;\n    }\n    return true;\n}\n\nbool validPalindrome(string s) {\n    int left = 0, right = (int)s.size() - 1;\n    while (left < right) {\n        if (s[left] != s[right]) {\n            // One deletion allowed: drop the left character or the right one, and check the rest.\n            return isPal(s, left + 1, right) || isPal(s, left, right - 1);\n        }\n        left++;\n        right--;\n    }\n    return true;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(1).** The outer loop and the two checks together look at each character at most about three times, and nothing is copied."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Brute force: try deleting every character",
          "time": "O(n²)",
          "timeWhy": "**n** candidate strings, each built and checked in **O(n)**.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "One candidate string."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Two pointers, two tries at the first mismatch",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "Each character is looked at **at most about three times**.",
          "space": "O(1)",
          "spaceWhy": "Just the **two pointers**; nothing is copied."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The insight that makes approach 2 work — *only the first mismatch matters* — is exactly what interviewers look for. Say it out loud before coding."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Already a palindrome** — no deletion: `true`.",
        "**The deletion is on the right** — `\"eeeed\"`: skipping the left `e` fails, skipping the `d` works. Both tries are needed.",
        "**Two deletions needed** — `\"abc\"`: `false`.",
        "**Length 1 or 2** — always `true`: delete one character of a pair if needed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Valid Palindrome III** — up to k deletions: that becomes dynamic programming — the longest palindromic subsequence must be at least n - k long.",
        "**Valid Palindrome** — no deletions allowed. Previous lesson.",
        "**Break a Palindrome** — change one character to make a palindrome the smallest non-palindrome: greedy over the first half."
      ]
    }
  ],
